## The first attempt at the BACKEND (not the gates) failed, twice, usefully
#
#   1. gen2 refused tools/native32.sa itself: "unexpected '\"'". Cause: a '{'
#      inside a string literal inside a `when` CONDITION is read by gen2 as
#      the block opener. Worked around with chr(123)/chr(125); recorded in
#      docs/FULL_LANGUAGE_SELFHOST.md and docs/NATIVE32.md.
#   2. The first expr.sa fixture used bare `show a == 2`, which gen2 refuses
#      (a parenthesised `show (a == 2)` is accepted). The fixture now uses
#      the parenthesised form so that all four backends can run it, and the
#      divergence is noted in the fixture header.
#
# Neither was a code-generation bug: once the file compiled, the emitted i386
# matched seed-min on every fixture at the first run.

